{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1837","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Bracket Coloring"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A regular bracket sequence is a bracket sequence that can be transformed into a correct arithmetic expression by inserting characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" between the original characters of the sequence. For example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the bracket sequences \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are regular (the resulting expressions are: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(1)+(1)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"((1+1)+1)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the bracket sequences \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are not. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A bracket sequence is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if one of the following conditions is satisfied:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" it is a regular bracket sequence; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if the order of the characters in this sequence is reversed, it becomes a regular bracket sequence. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the bracket sequences \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"()()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(())"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")))((("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"))()(("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are beautiful."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a bracket sequence $$$s$$$. You have to color it in such a way that:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" every bracket is colored into one color; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for every color, there is at least one bracket colored into that color; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for every color, if you write down the sequence of brackets having that color in the order they appear, you will get a beautiful bracket sequence. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Color the given bracket sequence $$$s$$$ into the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of colors according to these constraints, or report that it is impossible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of two lines. The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of characters in $$$s$$$. The second line contains $$$s$$$ — a string of $$$n$$$ characters, where each character is either \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"("}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Additional constraint on the input: the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if it is impossible to color the brackets according to the problem statement, print $$$-1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise, print two lines. In the first line, print one integer $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$) — the minimum number of colors. In the second line, print $$$n$$$ integers $$$c_1, c_2, \\dots, c_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le c_i \\le k$$$), where $$$c_i$$$ is the color of the $$$i$$$-th bracket. If there are multiple answers, print any of them. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"c